From 2f11b1a3286972f07c50d8b16a621418e7676c06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:54:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(post): a Sodick LN2W wire post and a Sodick AQ600L
 machine file

A second post script, sodick-ln2w.cps ("Sodick Wire EDM (LN2W)"), stands
beside the Mark 21 script, which has no change. Each cut starts in the
order that the owner of an AQ600L gave: G00 X Y, Z0., T91, T84, T94, the
C word, U0. V0., then the first G01. The post writes no G20 or G21 (the
LN2W control alarms on G21) and posts millimetre documents only.

A constant taper posts as TP / TN before the positioning move, G51 / G52
with A before the first leaning move and G50 before the move that stands
the wire upright. The new machine key edm.table_to_part_bottom and the
new stream parameter WireBottom give the two heights. Without the key
the taper is refused by name.

The new machine file sodick-aq600l.mch names the LN2W post. Its travel
figures are not yet checked against a published source: the decision
file says so. The EDM test parts square, 2-axis and taper are posted as
goldens under crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-ln2w/.

Fixes #4045

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
