+`sodick-ln2w.cps` (#4045, "Sodick Wire EDM (LN2W)") is the fifth
+`WIRE_POSTS` entry, never the default of the kind; `sodick-aq600l.mch`
+names it as its post. It is a file of its own beside `sodick-wire.cps`
+(the engine has no include; the Mark 21 file is not changed). It writes
+each cut in the order that the owner of an AQ600L gave: `G00 X Y`, `Z0.`,
+`T91`, `T84` / `T85`, `T94` / `T89`, the `C` word, `U0. V0.`, then `G01`.
+It writes no `G20` / `G21` (the control alarms on `G21`) and declares
+`programUnits = "mm"`. A constant taper on an angle-word machine
+(`edm.taper_angle`) posts as `TP` / `TN` before the positioning move
+(from `edm.table_to_part_bottom` and `PARAM WirePlane` / `WireBottom`),
+`G51` / `G52` with `A` before the first leaning move and `G50` before
+the move that stands the wire upright. It refuses by name a taper
+without those heights, a U V lean, 4-axis, any `COMP` record and an arc
+with the wire leaning. It was not run on a control in this form;
+`docs/decisions/4045-sodick-ln2w-dialect.md` lists what is confirmed and
+what is inferred. Its goldens ride under `nc/sodick-ln2w/`
+(`sodick_aq600l.rs`); its synthetic-stream pins are
+`crates/post/tests/sodick_ln2w.rs`.
+
