From 5bd7ff4ddc8ebc472abbafa76d7afb3f5a023025 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:35:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(post): Sodick LN2W - U0. V0. on the start rapid,
 refuse taper, AQ600L U/V 80 mm

Round 3 of PR #4065, from the review of head b12db2f06 and the owner's
round-2 correction:

- The start of each cut is G00 X Y U0. V0. (one line), Z0., T91, T84,
  T94, C..., then the first cut. No separate U0. V0. line.
- The LN2W post refuses each taper by name (#4075): TP / TN need the
  setup's height above the worktable, and the control's corner motion,
  lean side and angle precision are not confirmed. The taper code and
  edm.table_to_part_bottom / PARAM WireBottom are removed; the taper
  test part is pinned as a refusal.
- sodick-aq600l.mch: U/V 80 x 80 mm (Sodick AQ400L / AQ600L brochure),
  guide span 100 mm (a 20 deg lean fits the 40 mm half travel), no
  unconfirmed edm.taper_angle rule.
- The kernel STEP bench reads testdata/models/edm/ and pins its three
  files; a new STEP subdirectory with no bench fails it.
- assets/posts/AGENTS.md names the real pin paths.

The Mark 21 post and its goldens have no change.

Refs #4045, #4075

